window.EN={"1":"Grannvale, the great nation at the center of the continent of Jugdral, was","2":"founded by Saint Heim, one of the Twelve Crusaders.","3":"This nation is home not only to the royal family, descendants of Heim,","4":"but also to six Grand Duchies, which likewise carry the blood of the Crusaders.","5":"As lords of vast domains and their own armies,","6":"the duchies kept their own independence even while remaining subject to the kingdom.","7":"The kingdom's government, in place of the aging King Azmur,","8":"was run by the brilliant Prince Kurth,","9":"aided by Lord Byron, head of House Chalphy, who had the prince's deep trust,","10":"together with Lord Ring of House Jungby.","11":"Lord Reptor of House Freege, who held the position of chancellor,","12":"felt his own position threatened","13":"and drew in Lord Langobalt of the greedy House Dozel,","14":"forming a faction opposed to the prince.","15":"Lord Arvis, the young head of House Velthomer,","16":"did not involve himself in politics, holding the post of commander of the royal guard protecting the king,","17":"and only Father Claude of House Edda alone felt uneasy about the kingdom's dangerous state.","18":"Around that time, urgent news arrived from the east.","19":"Darna, a friendly city in the Yied Desert, had been invaded by the eastern barbarians of Isaach,","20":"and its people, it was said, had been slaughtered.","21":"Voices across the country rose up calling for the barbarians to be punished, and at last, the decision was made to subjugate Isaach.","22":"Prince Kurth, in place of his aging father King Azmur,","23":"led the nation's lords out to war.","24":"By his side, as always, was the man known as a valiant warrior—","25":"Lord Byron.","26":"After the expeditionary force departed, only a scant few soldiers remained in Grannvale, but","27":"to the west, on the border, lay Agustria,","28":"and to the southwest, the Kingdom of Verdane—both allied nations,","29":"so there should have been no cause for concern from behind.","30":"But that expectation was betrayed all too easily.","31":"A great army of the Kingdom of Verdane, led by Prince Gandolf,","32":"suddenly broke through the border and laid siege to Jungby Castle.","33":"The only one left to guard House Jungby was its daughter, Edain, alone.","34":"Sigurd, prince of the Duchy of Chalphy, who had been entrusted with the kingdom's defense by his father Lord Byron and had remained at the castle with a handful of men,","35":"was stunned by this news.","36":"Princess Edain was his childhood friend.","37":"\"I cannot hand her over to those barbarians.\"","38":"Prince Sigurd resolved at once to march out.","39":"In the year 757 of the Grannvale calendar... thus, the gate of destiny was opened.","40":"That this would, in time, become the harbinger of a terrible chain of events,","41":"no one, at that moment, had any way of knowing.","42":"Lady Edain, the enemy has surrounded the castle. We who should be protecting you, princess, have been so powerless...","43":"It's all right, Mideel... Everyone fought so well. Don't worry about me anymore.","44":"Right now, even if it's just one person, please—live on.","45":"No, Lady Edain. Everyone is resolved to protect you, princess, to the very end.","46":"Even at the cost of our lives, we will protect you.","47":"Thank you, Mideel... ...I'm sorry.","48":"Jungby Castle has been surrounded by Gandolf's army. At this rate, Edain is in danger.","49":"Noish, I'm going to go save her. I'm leaving the rest to you!","50":"Please wait, Lord Sigurd. Surely you don't mean to go alone?","51":"The main force of our army went on the expedition to Isaach with Father. Only a few of us remain here.","52":"The Verdane army may be barbarians, but it's a large force. I can't drag all of you into a fight where death is certain.","53":"Don't talk nonsense. Having been born a knight, dying in battle is only natural.","54":"We can't just sit back and let our lord die alone. We're coming with you too.","55":"Alec, you feel the same way, don't you?","56":"Ah, of course. But Jungby Castle matters, sure, but shouldn't saving the villages come first?","57":"They say the barbarians are raiding every village in their path, plundering, killing, and burning it all to the ground.","58":"We ought to go around the villages and strengthen their defenses before it's too late, don't you think?","59":"You're right. Protecting the people is our duty as knights. Well said, Alec.","60":"Nah, honestly, it was Oifey's idea.","61":"No wonder—grandson of the famed tactician Lord Shuhal. Even though he's still a kid, he notices all sorts of things.","62":"Is Oifey here at the castle? Oifey, if you're here, come out.","63":"Lord Sigurd, I'm sorry for coming without permission. But if you're marching out, please take me with you too.","64":"I don't want to just stay behind and watch the castle.","65":"But you're still a child. Will you be all right?","66":"I've already turned fourteen. I still can't fight, but I can at least take care of things for you, Lord Sigurd.","67":"Please—I'm begging you. Please keep me by your side.","68":"All right, Oifey. It's been two years since you came to me as a knight-in-training.","69":"It wouldn't hurt for you to experience the battlefield by now. But it's still too soon for you to fight.","70":"For a while, just stay by my side and be someone I can talk things over with.","71":"Yes! Thank you very much!","72":"Lord Sigurd, what will we do about defending this castle?","73":"Someone needs to stay on defense, or it's dangerous. If our home base, this castle, falls to the enemy, we're finished.","74":"Noish, there's nobody better for defending the castle than this guy! Right, Arden?","75":"Hey, Alec, why me?","76":"Tough, strong, and slow! You're the only one with all three!","77":"Tough and strong, fine, but I don't appreciate the \"slow\" part.","78":"No, Arden—I'm asking you myself too. You're the only one I can trust to guard the castle.","79":"Hah, fine, I get it. I'll go up and defend it for now. But let me go out and fight sometimes too, all right?","80":"Good, then let's go. For now, we help the villages. And then—on to Jungby!","81":"You lot, how much longer are you gonna drag this out with such a tiny castle... Damn it, I'll do it myself.","82":"Heh heh... You put up a good fight all on your own, kid. But this is as far as you go—take this!","83":"Guh... Lady Edain... forgive me.","84":"Ahh, Mideel...","85":"Ohh, now this is quite the prize. The princess of Jungby, is it... heh heh... All right, I'll take this woman back to my country.","86":"Leave the rest to you and Gerald.","87":"Heh...","88":"Don't worry. I'll head back with my brother Kinbois's army.","89":"Then we'll march all the way up to Belhalla—after all, there's no army left in this country right now.","90":"We can do whatever we want.","91":"Yessir, understood, leave it to us!","92":"Hey, don't you dawdle! Walk, and quick about it!!","93":".........","94":"Knock down the bridge so the Grannvale lot can't follow us in!","95":"Yessir, understood.","96":"Hey, Gerald, I'm heading back to Marfa Castle. I'm leaving this castle to you, so guard it well.","97":"Yessir, understood. But Prince Gandolf, who is this woman?","98":"My spoils of war. I'll take her back to Marfa and make her my wife. Not bad, eh?","99":"Heh, I can't help but drool just looking at her.","100":"Fool, don't make that greedy face. Once we've occupied Grannvale, I'll give you all you want too.","101":"Until then, be patient.","102":"You people are beasts... God, please—give these people the hearts of human beings...","103":"What are you muttering about? Come on, let's go! Don't dawdle!!","104":"Go on, men! Chalphy's next! While we're at it, grab the villages' treasure too!","105":"Lex, looks like we made it in time somehow.","106":"Yeah, Prince Sigurd seems to be having a rough time against Verdane's big army.","107":"He'll be glad we came. But you're a strange one too—you could've just left it alone.","108":"Our country's main forces are off on the expedition to Isaach. Almost nobody's left in the homeland.","109":"Prince Sigurd is trying to fight to the death with just the handful of soldiers left in Chalphy.","110":"I can't just abandon him.","111":"Heh... You're as dishonest with yourself as ever. That's not the only reason, is it?","112":"Wh-what are you talking about!","113":"You're worried about Princess Edain of Jungby. I know you like her.","114":"Y-you're talking nonsense!","115":"See, your face is already turning red. Ha, you're a cute one.","116":"L-Lex! Cut it out already! I'm going on ahead!","117":"Ha ha ha, all right, all right. Guess I'll show off a bit of my own strength here too.","118":"Looks like we made it. Is Sigurd safe?","119":"Yes, my brother should be fine... But he doesn't have anyone with him who can use magic,","120":"so I'm sure he's in trouble. I wanted to help him with my heal staff...","121":"I'm sorry, Quan, for making even you fight.","122":"I'm a woman married into House Leonster now, no longer one of Chalphy's own, but it was too painful just to watch quietly...","123":"On my brother's behalf, let me thank you.","124":"No need for thanks, Ethlyn. Sigurd is a dear friend to me too.","125":"And now that I've made you my wife, he's my brother-in-law as well. I won't let you fight alone.","126":"Thank you... Quan.","127":"Let's hurry, Lord Quan, Lady Ethlyn. The battlefield is probably just ahead.","128":"Prince Sigurd, I'm glad to see you safe.","129":"You're Prince Azel of House Velthomer? Why are you here?","130":"I wanted to be of some help, even a little, in the fight against Verdane, so I rushed here with Lex.","131":"Please allow us to fight alongside you as well.","132":"Of course, nothing could please me more. But does your older brother—Lord Arvis—know about this?","133":"No... My brother's been entrusted with command of the royal guard, as the king's close aide.","134":"I was told firmly that I must never leave the capital, Belhalla, either.","135":"I'd imagine so. But then won't you be scolded for this later?","136":"It's hard to say, but... I'm afraid of my brother. Just being near him makes it feel hard to breathe...","137":"Besides... a no-good little brother like me is nothing but a burden to him anyway...","138":"I see... sounds like there's a lot going on there. But I'm glad you came—it gives me courage. If you don't mind, I'd like you to stay as long as you like.","139":"Yes!","140":"He really is just like the rumors say... nothing at all like my brother...","141":"Prince Sigurd, it's been a while.","142":"Lex! You came to help too?","143":"Azel practically dragged me along. Honestly, what a pain.","144":"Ha, still as sharp-tongued as ever. But does your father, Lord Langobalt, know about this?","145":"No way. My old man's got it in for your father something fierce,","146":"there's no way he'd allow helping Chalphy. I came on my own.","147":"Just so there's no misunderstanding—it's not for your sake. My best friend Azel asked, so I came.","148":"Ha, that's harsh... but I'm grateful. Really, thank you.","149":"...Well, I'll do what I can. Can't let those Verdane barbarians just do as they please.","150":"Sigurd, you're safe!","151":"Prince Quan! Why are you here...","152":"I heard about the fight with Verdane and couldn't just leave it be. I wanted to help too.","153":"But is the Kingdom of Leonster all right? I heard Thracia has its eye on it?","154":"That's true, which is why I could only bring Finn. I left my Lance Knights in Father's care.","155":"I see... I'm sorry, Quan, for dragging you into trouble too.","156":"What are you saying, Sigurd. This is what we promised each other, isn't it?","157":"Eh...?","158":"When we were boys, the three of us—you, Eldigan of the Kingdom of Nodion, and I—","159":"met at the officers' academy in the capital, Belhalla.","160":"And we talked about our dreams together and swore to help each other no matter what.","161":"That's right... I haven't forgotten either...","162":"Verdane's barbarians will be driven off in no time if we work together.","163":"Sigurd, don't forget—I will never allow you to be lost in a battle like this.","164":"Brother, you're safe!!","165":"Ethlyn, it's been a while. Thank you for coming.","166":"When I heard Verdane had attacked, I was so, so worried... but I'm glad, you look well.","167":"Ethlyn, did you really think I'd lose to the likes of Verdane?","168":"Well, I'd heard only a handful of soldiers were left in Chalphy.","169":"Brother, you've always been reckless.","170":"I thought I had to come help in Father's place, while he's away on the expedition...","171":"Heh, you've always been so dependable.","172":"In place of our mother, who passed away when we were young, you looked after Father and me.","173":"I thought marrying into the royal house of Leonster might have made you a bit more ladylike, but you haven't changed one bit.","174":"Quan must have a hard time of it too, ha ha...","175":"Brother...! The reason I got so naggy is because of you and Father.","176":"Because the two of you are so careless...","177":"Ha, maybe that's true. Ethlyn... I really am grateful to you.","178":"I really am sorry about this whole thing too. I don't know how to thank you...","179":"Brother...","180":"[Only if visited as Sigurd]","181":"Lord Sigurd, once you've rested, please go meet the people of the town.","182":"If they see you looking well, Lord Sigurd, I think the townspeople will feel reassured.","183":"Ah, thank you so much for coming. Our village is saved now.","184":"This money was collected from the villagers. It's not much, but please put it to use in the fight.","185":"If you can save the other villages too, I'm sure they'll want to help you as well.","186":"Listen well—the sword is strong against the axe, the axe is strong against the lance, and the lance is strong against the sword.","187":"Think carefully about these matchups when you fight.","188":"And if you're wounded, it's good to go to a church—just a little rest there, and you'll heal right up.","189":"Mind you, it's not free. It costs 5 gold per 1 HP.","190":"The House of Chalphy that rules this land has been famous for generations as swordsmen, you know.","191":"After all, they carry the blood of Baldr, the god of light.","192":"Those Verdane barbarians—if only Lord Byron had his holy sword Tyrfing, he'd finish them off in no time.","193":"This place, Jungby, is a house known for archery. The duke's family descends from Ulir, the god of bows.","194":"Duke Ring had twin sisters, and below them, a son,","195":"but the elder of the twin sisters was carried off by pirates when she was young, and she's still missing to this day.","196":"Lady Edain's younger brother, Lord Andrey, is away on the expedition with his father, Duke Ring, but I haven't heard good rumors about him.","197":"Seems the relationship between father and son has gone cold too...","198":"Oh, you've finally come to help us. I thought it was hopeless. Here, let me give you this ring as thanks.","199":"It's called a Speed Ring. It's a strange bracelet—just wearing it raises your Speed.","200":"Here, try putting it on. This should make it harder for enemies to land their attacks on you.","201":"So you've come, you Grannvale cowards. I'll finish you all off myself!","202":"This... this can't be happening...","203":"Lord Sigurd, a young knight has fallen here!","204":"Hm...? Ah, isn't that Mideel? What happened—stay with me!","205":"Ugh... ...you're... ...Lord Sigurd.","206":"Mideel, are you all right!? What happened to Edain?","207":"I don't know... probably... Gandolf took her...","208":"I see... Don't worry, Mideel. I'll get Edain back. You just rest and heal.","209":"No, Lord Sigurd, I'm coming too. I can't rest at all with Lady Edain on my mind!","210":"What, Demazio failed!? Entrusted with the castle by Prince Gandolf, and he's useless for anything!","211":"Damn it, repair the bridge over the Jung River—we're attacking again!","212":"His Majesty asked me to come check on things, but to think you'd struggle this much against mere barbarians.","213":"Sigurd... so this is all you amount to after all...","214":"[If Azel is alive]","215":"Prince Sigurd, it's been a while.","216":"Lord Arvis!? Why are you here...","217":"His Majesty was worried and ordered me to come see how things were.","218":"And this—this is something His Majesty has bestowed on you. Please take it.","219":"This is the Silver Sword!... His Majesty, giving this to me... ah, what an honor.","220":"Lord Arvis, please tell His Majesty that Sigurd is deeply grateful.","221":"Understood. By the way, Sigurd, I heard that my brother Azel has joined your army. Is that true?","222":"I'm sorry, he seems to have come without telling you, but I couldn't turn him away.","223":"If possible, I'd like him to stay with my army for a while.","224":"I see... no, as long as he's safe, that's fine. Azel may have a different mother, but he's still my one and only precious little brother.","225":"I'd rather have him by my side, but I suppose it can't be helped...","226":"Sigurd, I leave Azel in your hands. Please teach him all sorts of things.","227":"Leave it to me. Once this battle is over, I'll try to persuade him to go back myself.","228":"Hearing that puts me at ease. Well, I'll be heading back to the capital, Belhalla. I must protect His Majesty, after all.","229":"Sigurd, I'll leave the rest to you.","230":"[If Azel has died]","231":"Prince Sigurd, it's been a while.","232":"Lord Arvis!?... Why are you here...","233":"His Majesty was worried and ordered me to come see how things were.","234":"And this—this is something His Majesty has bestowed on you. Please take it.","235":"This is the Silver Sword!... His Majesty, giving this to me... ah, what an honor.","236":"Lord Arvis, please tell His Majesty that Sigurd is deeply grateful.","237":"Understood. By the way, Sigurd, I heard my brother Azel joined your army—is he safe?","238":"That... Azel is...","239":"You mean he died in battle?","240":"I'm sorry... it's because my strength wasn't enough...","241":"Azel... what a foolish little brother...","242":"[If fought against Mideel]","243":"W-wait! Using ranged weapons is such a coward's trick!","244":"Silence! Where have you taken Lady Edain! Give her back, now!!","245":"[If fought against any other unit]","246":"You Grannvale dogs, drop dead!","247":"Too bad for you... that woman isn't here. By now, she's probably with Prince Gandolf...","248":"Lord Sigurd, I searched every corner of the castle, but Lady Edain is nowhere to be found.","249":"What... Where on earth could Edain be...","250":"She was likely taken away by Verdane before the castle fell... I hope she's safe.","251":"Guh... unforgivable... as long as they don't give Edain back, I'll chase them to the ends of the earth.","252":"Lord Sigurd, a messenger from the king has arrived from Belhalla.","253":"Lord Sigurd, this battle was a splendid victory.","254":"His Majesty was greatly pleased and has bestowed upon you the title of Royal Holy Knight.","255":"An honor beyond what I deserve. I swear even greater loyalty to His Majesty.","256":"And this is important: the castle must not be taken by the enemy. As long as the castle remains standing to the end,","257":"you'll continue receiving war funds, but each time it's destroyed by the enemy, that amount will be reduced.","258":"Please take care in the battles to come as well."};
